### Digital Signage backend -- curl / .http test collection
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy each curl
### equivalent (given as a comment above each block) into a shell.
###
### Set these before running:
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@deviceId = tv-sucursal-centro-01
@adminIdToken = PASTE_A_FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN_HERE

### 1) Register a brand-new device (idempotent -- safe to re-run).
# curl -s -X POST "$BASE_URL/register" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"deviceId":"tv-sucursal-centro-01","screenWidth":1920,"screenHeight":1080}'
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}",
  "screenWidth": 1920,
  "screenHeight": 1080
}

### 2) Get the playlist for a pending (unpaired) device -- expect items: [].
# curl -s "$BASE_URL/playlist?deviceId=tv-sucursal-centro-01"
GET {{baseUrl}}/playlist?deviceId={{deviceId}}

### 3) After pairing in the admin panel (see /admin/pairing below), fetch the
### playlist again -- capture the ETag response header for the next call.
# curl -si "$BASE_URL/playlist?deviceId=tv-sucursal-centro-01" -H "X-Device-Key: dk_xxx"
GET {{baseUrl}}/playlist?deviceId={{deviceId}}
X-Device-Key: dk_REPLACE_WITH_ISSUED_KEY

### 4) Demonstrate 304 Not Modified: resend the same ETag via If-None-Match.
### Expect: HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified, empty body.
# curl -si "$BASE_URL/playlist?deviceId=tv-sucursal-centro-01" \
#   -H "X-Device-Key: dk_xxx" -H 'If-None-Match: "PASTE_ETAG_FROM_STEP_3"'
GET {{baseUrl}}/playlist?deviceId={{deviceId}}
X-Device-Key: dk_REPLACE_WITH_ISSUED_KEY
If-None-Match: "PASTE_ETAG_FROM_STEP_3"

### 5) Heartbeat -- always returns 204 immediately (writes are async/batched).
# curl -si -X POST "$BASE_URL/heartbeat" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{
#   "deviceId":"tv-sucursal-centro-01","appVersion":"1.4.2","itemActual":"2",
#   "uptime":3600.5,"ultimoError":null,"screenWidth":1920,"screenHeight":1080}'
POST {{baseUrl}}/heartbeat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}",
  "appVersion": "1.4.2",
  "itemActual": "2",
  "uptime": 3600.5,
  "ultimoError": null,
  "screenWidth": 1920,
  "screenHeight": 1080
}

### --- Admin API (all require a Firebase ID token for an allow-listed email) ---

### 6) Who am I (sanity check for the bearer token / allow-list).
# curl -s "$BASE_URL/admin/whoami" -H "Authorization: Bearer $ID_TOKEN"
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### 7) Pair the pending device created in step 1 (use the 6-digit pairingCode
### returned by /register).
# curl -s -X POST "$BASE_URL/admin/pairing" -H "Authorization: Bearer $ID_TOKEN" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"pairingCode":"123456","nombre":"Sucursal Centro","groupId":"norte"}'
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/pairing
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pairingCode": "123456",
  "nombre": "Sucursal Centro",
  "groupId": "norte"
}

### 8) List devices.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### 9) Send a command to a device.
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/devices/{{deviceId}}/command
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "command": "reload"
}

### 10) Dashboard summary.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### --- Scheduler-triggered job endpoints (normally called by Cloud Scheduler
### with an OIDC token; for local testing set SCHEDULER_DEV_SHARED_SECRET in
### backend/.env and pass it via X-Scheduler-Key instead). ---

### 11) Mark stale devices offline.
# curl -s -X POST "$BASE_URL/jobs/mark-offline-devices" -H "X-Scheduler-Key: local-dev-secret"
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/mark-offline-devices
X-Scheduler-Key: local-dev-secret

### 12) Hourly device snapshot into BigQuery.
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/snapshot-devices
X-Scheduler-Key: local-dev-secret

### 13) Daily heartbeat purge.
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/purge-old-heartbeats
X-Scheduler-Key: local-dev-secret
